From 528c6eae2a3dfced741a564be8b655de7f8e3274 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nex <63727521+LuCiLuna@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 10:27:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 092/114] WIP: drm/panel: amb670yf01: expose 1440x3216 and
 1080x2412 at 60/90/120 Hz

The panel's native resolution is 1440x3216; 1080x2412 is the vendor's
scaled mode, which this driver had hardcoded along with a refresh rate.
Offer all of the vendor's timings, 1440x3216 at 120 Hz being preferred.
They differ in a few init commands, and in the DSC slices: 720x24 for
1440x3216 and 540x36 for 1080x2412.

DSI hosts take a single DSC config from the panel, and msm rejects modes
which aren't a multiple of its slices. HACK: add a mode_set callback to
mipi_dsi_device, which msm calls with a new mode while the display is off,
so the panel can update its DSC config before msm uses it, and skip the
slice check on such panels.

Set hfp so the bit clock derived by msm gives the vendor's panel clockrate:
this was off on 1080x2412 at 60 Hz, as hfp had been worked out for 10 bpc.

Tested switching between all modes with wlr-randr.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
